1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,043
A content field is a named, typed piece of data that a content part carries.

2
00:00:06,043 --> 00:00:09,241
In this video, you read the pieces of a field:

3
00:00:09,241 --> 00:00:12,992
its class, display driver, views, settings and editors.

4
00:00:12,992 --> 00:00:15,760
Then you see them at work in the admin.

5
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:24,014
A content field is a class that inherits from Content Field.

6
00:00:24,014 --> 00:00:28,167
Its properties are the data, saved as JSON in the content item, under

7
00:00:28,167 --> 00:00:31,710
the part that carries the field, by the name of the field.

8
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:35,269
The class does not say where it is used.

9
00:00:35,269 --> 00:00:40,153
A part definition lists its fields, with a technical name, a display name,

10
00:00:40,153 --> 00:00:43,450
an editor, a display mode and settings for each.

11
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:47,480
A content type keeps its own fields in a part with its name.

12
00:00:48,230 --> 00:00:50,050
Four pieces make a field:

13
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:54,630
the class that holds the data, a display driver that displays, edits and

14
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:59,973
updates it, views that draw each shape, and a settings driver that edits the options.

15
00:00:59,973 --> 00:01:02,850
Registration in Startup ties them together.

16
00:01:07,050 --> 00:01:12,190
Take the Boolean field of the Content Fields module, which has all four pieces.

17
00:01:12,190 --> 00:01:16,545
Its class inherits from Content Field and has one property, Value.

18
00:01:16,545 --> 00:01:21,020
The content item serializes that property with the rest of its data.

19
00:01:21,770 --> 00:01:28,079
Settings are a second class, inheriting from Field Settings, which already has Hint and Required.

20
00:01:28,079 --> 00:01:31,570
The Boolean field adds a Label and a Default Value.

21
00:01:31,570 --> 00:01:35,980
They belong to the definition of the field, not to a content item.

22
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:45,404
The display driver inherits from Content Field Display Driver of the field type.

23
00:01:45,404 --> 00:01:51,538
Display builds the front end, Edit builds the editor, and Update Async applies the posted form.

24
00:01:51,538 --> 00:01:54,150
Each method returns a display result.

25
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:59,172
Display creates a shape, which a template renders, with Initialize.

26
00:01:59,172 --> 00:02:03,619
Get Display Shape Type names it after the field type and display mode,

27
00:02:03,619 --> 00:02:06,076
and the lambda fills its view model.

28
00:02:06,076 --> 00:02:11,050
Location puts it in the Content zone, for the Detail and Summary display types.

29
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:15,912
Edit builds the editor shape the same way, and Get Editor Shape Type

30
00:02:15,912 --> 00:02:18,190
adds the chosen editor to the name.

31
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:23,246
For an item that is being created, the value starts from the default in the settings.

32
00:02:23,246 --> 00:02:25,580
Otherwise, it starts from the field.

33
00:02:26,330 --> 00:02:29,561
Update Async copies the posted value into the field.

34
00:02:29,561 --> 00:02:34,353
The prefix, built from the part name and the field name, keeps form names apart.

35
00:02:34,353 --> 00:02:35,690
Return the editor:

36
00:02:35,690 --> 00:02:40,370
the base class applies the field to its part only when the result is not null.

37
00:02:44,570 --> 00:02:46,571
Each shape has a view model.

38
00:02:46,571 --> 00:02:50,808
The editor one carries the value to bind, with the field, its part

39
00:02:50,808 --> 00:02:52,926
and its part field definition.

40
00:02:52,926 --> 00:02:56,810
The display one exposes the same value, read from the field.

41
00:02:57,560 --> 00:03:00,438
A template's file name gives its shape type:

42
00:03:00,438 --> 00:03:04,986
Boolean Field is the front end, and Boolean Field dot Edit is the editor.

43
00:03:04,986 --> 00:03:09,304
The editor template binds a checkbox to Value, and labels it with the

44
00:03:09,304 --> 00:03:12,700
Label setting or, if empty, the field's display name.

45
00:03:13,450 --> 00:03:17,694
The display template prints the value inside a div, with a class made

46
00:03:17,694 --> 00:03:19,732
from the part and field names.

47
00:03:19,732 --> 00:03:24,033
Templates in the Views folder of an enabled feature are found by their

48
00:03:24,033 --> 00:03:26,240
file names, with no registration.

49
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:36,188
A settings driver inherits from Content Part Field Definition Display Driver of the field type.

50
00:03:36,188 --> 00:03:40,969
Edit builds the settings editor with Initialize, fills it from Get Settings of

51
00:03:40,969 --> 00:03:45,010
the part field definition, and places it in the Content location.

52
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:48,886
Update Async reads the form into a settings object.

53
00:03:48,886 --> 00:03:53,165
With Settings, on the builder, stores it in the definition of the field.

54
00:03:53,165 --> 00:03:58,430
Returning Edit gives back the editor, which the page shows again when the form has errors.

55
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:03,456
The settings view is a template named after its shape, with one input

56
00:04:03,456 --> 00:04:06,706
each for the hint, the label and the default value.

57
00:04:06,706 --> 00:04:11,780
The admin shows them as Hint, Label, and a check box labeled Default value is true.

58
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:20,493
In the Startup class of your module, Add Content Field registers the type.

59
00:04:20,493 --> 00:04:25,344
Use Display Driver attaches the display driver to every editor and display mode.

60
00:04:25,344 --> 00:04:30,760
The settings driver is a scoped service of I Content Part Field Definition Display Driver.

61
00:04:31,510 --> 00:04:35,231
Registering the type is what lists it under Field Type when you add

62
00:04:35,231 --> 00:04:36,863
a field to a content type.

63
00:04:36,863 --> 00:04:40,737
Depend on the Content Types feature in the manifest of your module, as

64
00:04:40,737 --> 00:04:42,623
the Content Fields module does.

65
00:04:42,623 --> 00:04:45,070
A separate video covers creating a module.

66
00:04:49,270 --> 00:04:51,539
A field can have several editors.

67
00:04:51,539 --> 00:04:55,147
The Switch editor of the Boolean field is two templates.

68
00:04:55,147 --> 00:04:59,628
The one named Boolean Field, a dash, Switch, dot Edit draws the switch,

69
00:04:59,628 --> 00:05:03,410
and its Option template adds Switch to the list of editors.

70
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:06,004
The driver does not change.

71
00:05:06,004 --> 00:05:09,915
Get Editor Shape Type adds the editor name to the shape type, so

72
00:05:09,915 --> 00:05:15,390
the Switch template is found, and Use Display Driver registered the driver for every editor.

73
00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:21,609
Display modes follow the same pattern, with a Display template and a Display Option template.

74
00:05:21,609 --> 00:05:24,923
An editor or a display mode can have its own settings.

75
00:05:24,923 --> 00:05:30,060
The Header mode of the Text field uses the Display Mode location for its heading level.

76
00:05:34,277 --> 00:05:37,436
The pieces on the slides show up in the admin.

77
00:05:37,436 --> 00:05:43,146
This Event content type has the Title and Autoroute parts, and its Fields list is empty.

78
00:05:43,146 --> 00:05:44,907
Let's select Add Field.

79
00:05:45,378 --> 00:05:50,108
The Field Type list holds every field type that an enabled module registered

80
00:05:50,108 --> 00:05:51,781
with Add Content Field.

81
00:05:51,781 --> 00:05:56,798
Let's name the field Featured, choose Boolean Field, and select Save & Configure.

82
00:05:57,250 --> 00:06:00,704
The settings page shows the settings of the Boolean field.

83
00:06:00,704 --> 00:06:04,643
Hint, Label and a check box labeled Default value is true come from

84
00:06:04,643 --> 00:06:07,880
the settings view, and the settings driver saves them.

85
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:10,470
Let's set a label, and tick the check box.

86
00:06:10,968 --> 00:06:14,181
The next label asks What type of editor should be used?

87
00:06:14,181 --> 00:06:17,710
Its list has one entry for each Option template of the field:

88
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:19,079
Standard and Switch.

89
00:06:19,079 --> 00:06:20,448
Let's choose Switch.

90
00:06:20,914 --> 00:06:24,555
The next label asks What type of display mode should be used?

91
00:06:24,555 --> 00:06:29,554
Its list has only Standard, because the Boolean field has one Display Option template.

92
00:06:29,554 --> 00:06:31,184
Let's save the settings.

93
00:06:31,634 --> 00:06:35,941
The type editor lists the field with its display name, its type, and

94
00:06:35,941 --> 00:06:38,094
a badge for its editor, Switch.

95
00:06:38,550 --> 00:06:40,279
Next, the content editor.

96
00:06:40,279 --> 00:06:44,352
The switch is on, because the item is being created and the default

97
00:06:44,352 --> 00:06:48,034
value is true, and its label is the one set in the settings.

98
00:06:48,034 --> 00:06:50,210
Let's enter a title, and publish.

99
00:06:50,673 --> 00:06:54,565
On the front end, the Content zone of the item holds the field,

100
00:06:54,565 --> 00:06:57,273
and the display template prints its value.

101
00:06:59,273 --> 00:07:01,041
That is a content field:

102
00:07:01,041 --> 00:07:05,993
a class, a display driver, views, settings and a registration in Startup, with

103
00:07:05,993 --> 00:07:09,000
editors and display modes added as templates.

104
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,533
Thanks for watching.

